nts\nPostdoctoral Researcher\nStaff\nNews\nEvents\nResearch\nResearch Areas\nResearch Centers and Groups\nSeminar Listing\nPhysical and Mathematical Sciences Library\nMathWeb\nInternal Math Calendar\nReserve a Room (McAllister)\nRoom Reservation Request (Outside McAllister)\nMy Teaching\nTravel Reimbursement Forms\nCopy Request Form for Teaching Purposes\nUndergrad Resources\nHosting a Visitor\nCommittees\nDepartment Policies\nNetwork Documentation\nSubmitted by sws139\non Tue, 10/29/2019 - 15:44\nGraduate Admission Requirements\nFrequently Asked Questions\nBreadcrumb\nDepartment of Mathematics\nGraduate Program\nGraduate Admission\nGraduate Admission FAQ\nmath\nAbout\nDepartment Administration\nContact Us\nGiving\nHiring\nMiscellaneous Resources\nMcAllister Building\nGraduate\nAdmissions\nPHD Program\nOther degrees\nCourses\nTeaching in Math\nMathematics at Penn State\nPh.D. Graduates\nUndergraduate\nWhy Choose Mathematics?\nMathematics Majors\nMathematics Minor\nMathematics Courses\nHonors Math\nMathematics Advising\nPenn State Math Club\nLearning Assistants\nGraders and Proctors\nResearch Opportunities\nPeople\nFaculty\nGraduate Faculty\nGraduate Students\nPostdoctoral Researcher\nStaff\nNews\nEvents\nResearch\nResearch Areas\nResearch Centers and Groups\nSeminar Listing\nPhysical and Mathematical Sciences Library\nMathWeb\nInternal Math Calendar\nReserve a Room (McAllister)\nRoom Reservation Request (Outside McAllister)\nMy Teaching\nTravel Reimbursement Forms\nCopy Request Form for Teaching Purposes\nUndergrad Resources\nHosting a Visitor\nCommittees\nDepartment Policies\nNetwork Documentation\ngraduate\nAdmissions\nOverview\nRequirements\nFellowships & Financial Aid\nGraduate Admission FAQ\nHow to apply\nPHD Program\nQualifying Exams\nOral and Written English Competency\nGraduate Student Seminar\nMath Graduate Handbook\nTransition Programs\nOther degrees\nCourses\n500-level graduate courses\nCourses for Research Areas\nCurrent Year Graduate Courses\nTeaching in Math\nMathematics at Penn State\nPh.D. Graduates\nFrequently Asked Questions about applying\nExpand All\nWhat is the application deadline?\nThe deadline each year is January 5th.\nIs it necessary to have a master's degree before applying to the Ph.D. program?\nNo, you may apply directly to the Ph.D. program without a master's degree.\nDo you offer Spring admissions?\nNo, our first-year graduate courses designed for Ph.D. qualifying examinations are two-semester courses. Granting Spring admissions would put students at a disadvantage.\nCan the application fee be waived?\nYes, under special circumstances we may be able to waive the fee. Please contact Katie Greenland kle16@psu.edu to request this.\nCan you send me a paper application?\nNo, paper applications are no longer accepted by the Graduate School. Applications must be submitted electronically.\nDo you supply/require forms for letters of recommendation?\nNo, we request plain text letters from your recommenders.\nAre you able to grant provisional admission if my TOEFL score is too low?\nNo, the TOEFL is a requirement of the Graduate School. A low TOEFL is not accepted by the International Student Services office when preparing visa documents.\nIs the Math Subject GRE required?\nScores for the Graduate Record Examination (GRE) are optional, not required for admission.\nWhat is the minimum TOEFL (Test of English as a Foreign Language) or IELTS (International English Language Testing System) score accepted?\nThis is a Graduate School requirement, and the minimum scores are:\nTOEFL\n550 (paper test)\n213 (computer-based test)\n80-19 on the speak section (internet-based test)\nIELTS\n6.5\nYear\nInternet-based\nPaper\nComputer-Based\n2019\n100.91\n2018\n89.75\n2017\n104.17\n2016\n96\n2015\n101\n2014\n96\n2013\n99\n2012\n88\n2011\n95\n2010\n95\n2009\n100\n2008\n98\n255\n2007\n618\n2006\n2005\n606\n262\n2004\n611\n258\n2003\n611\n258\n2002\n585\n2001\n608\n2000\n587\n240\nWhat is the minimum GPA required?\nWhile the Graduate School does not require a minimum GPA, it is generally expected that an applicant maintain a junior/senior GPA of 2.50 for admissions. The Department of Mathematics does not have a minimum score required.\nListed below are the average GPAs of students admitted to our program for the last several years.\nYear\nGPA\n2019\n3.70\n2018\n3.70\n2017\n3.78\n2016\n3.65\n2015\n3.75\n2014\n3.65\n2013\n3.89\n2012\n3.83\n2011\n3.62\n2010\n3.80\n2009\n3.67\n2008\n3.68\n2007\n3.74\n2006\n3.52\n2005\n3.75\n2004\n3.70\n2003\n3.65\n2002\n3.68\n2001\n3.74\n2000\n3.75\nMay I apply to more than one graduate program?\nNo, the Graduate School does not permit students to apply to more than one program at a time.\nI already have a Ph.D. in another area. May I apply to obtain a Ph.D. in a different area?\nThe Graduate School discourages the pursuit of a second doctorate:\nThe Graduate School does not admit applicants to concurrent double Ph.D. degree programs, D.Ed. degree programs, or concurrent Ph.D. and D.Ed. programs. In general, the Graduate School discourages the pursuit of a second Ph.D. or D.Ed. degree. However, if an applicant who holds either of these degrees requests admission to a second doctoral degree program (either Ph.D. or D.Ed.), the applicant is asked to give the Graduate School the reason why the second doctorate is necessary (as opposed to taking course work or a master's degree in the second field). The Graduate School may then solicit responses concerning the necessity of a second doctorate from representatives of the field at Penn State or elsewhere. This information is then given to the Dean of the Graduate School for the final decision. If approved, all Graduate School requirements for the second doctorate must be met de novo.\nThe justification for a second doctorate must be submitted to the Graduate School for consideration\u2014this is not a decision for the Department of Mathematics.\nCollege Resources\nAdministrative Offices\nCommunications\nData Services\nEmployment Opportunities\nFacilities\nCollege Resources 2\nFinance\nHuman Resources\nInformation Technology\nInstruction and Curricula\nResearch Administration\nResources\nOffices and Centers\nGrove Center for Excellence in Science Education\nOffice for Undergraduate Students\nOffice of Development and Alumni Relations\nOffice of Diversity and Inclusion\nOffice of Science Engagement\nOffice of Science Outreach\nStudent Programs\nAcademic Advising\nCo-op\nEducation Abroad\nInternship\nUndergraduate Research\nPennState-Eberly College of Science\nFooter Menu\nCollege Org. Chart\nHotline\nContact Us\nLog in\nFollow the Eberly College of Science\nCopyright \u00a9 , The Pennsylvania State University | Privacy and Legal Statements", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://science.psu.edu/math/graduate/admission/frequently-asked-questions#main-content"], ["News", "https://science.psu.edu/news"], ["Events", "https://science.psu.edu/events"], ["Development and Alumni Relations", "https://science.psu.edu/alumni-and-development"], ["Faculty and Staff Directory", "https://science.psu.edu/people"], ["", "https://science.psu.edu/"], ["News", "https://science.psu.edu/news"], ["Events", "https://science.psu.edu/events"], ["Development and Alumni Relations", "https://science.psu.edu/alumni-and-development"], ["Faculty and Staff Directory", "https://science.psu.edu/people"], ["About", "https://science.psu.edu/math"], ["Department Administration", "https://science.psu.edu/math/department-administration"], ["Contact Us", "https://science.psu.edu/math/contact-us"], ["Giving", "https://science.psu.edu/math/giving"], ["Hiring", "https://science.psu.edu/math/hiring"], ["Miscellaneous Resources", "https://science.psu.edu/math/miscellaneous-resources"], ["McAllister Building", "https://science.psu.edu/math/mcallister"], ["Graduate", "https://science.psu.edu/math/graduate"], ["Admissions", "https://science.psu.edu/math/graduate/admission"], ["PHD Program", "https://science.psu.edu/math/